# Rust Error Handling Standards

This codebase follows excellent error handling patterns. **ALWAYS** maintain these standards when writing or modifying Rust code.

## 1. Error Type Architecture

### Use `anyhow::Result<T>` in Backend Layers
```rust
// Domain, use cases, infrastructure - use anyhow::Result
use anyhow::{Result, Context, bail, anyhow};

fn process_image(...) -> Result<()> { ... }
fn create_video(...) -> Result<String> { ... }
```

### Convert to `Result<T, String>` at Command Boundaries
```rust
// Commands convert to String for frontend
#[tauri::command]
pub async fn create_video(...) -> Result<String, String> {
    use_case.execute(...)
        .await
        .map_err(|e| e.to_string()) // ALWAYS convert anyhow to String
}
```

## 2. Error Context Patterns

### Add Context with `.context()` and `.with_context()`
```rust
// Static context
std::fs::create_dir_all(output_dir)
    .with_context(|| format!("Failed to create output directory: {:?}", output_dir))?;

// Dynamic context with closure
validate_file_extension(image_path_buf)
    .with_context(|| format!("Invalid image file: {}", image_path))?;

// Simple context for external commands
cmd.output().with_context(|| {
    "Failed to execute ffmpeg command. Make sure ffmpeg is installed and in PATH."
})?;
```

## 3. Error Creation Patterns

### Use `anyhow::bail!()` for Early Returns
```rust
// Early validation failures
if main_path.is_none() && main_url.is_none() {
    anyhow::bail!("No image provided");
}

// Command validation failures
if !output.status.success() {
    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr);
    anyhow::bail!("FFmpeg error: {}", stderr);
}
```

### Use `anyhow::anyhow!()` for Error Creation
```rust
// Creating errors with context
Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Failed to create video for {}: {}", audio_path, e))

// Timeout errors
anyhow::anyhow!(
    "Image processing timed out after {} seconds",
    timeout::IMAGE_PROCESSING.as_secs()
)
```

## 4. Timeout Error Handling

### Wrap Blocking Operations with Descriptive Timeout Errors
```rust
tokio::time::timeout(timeout::IMAGE_PROCESSING, process_task)
    .await
    .map_err(|_| {
        anyhow::anyhow!(
            "Image processing timed out after {} seconds",
            timeout::IMAGE_PROCESSING.as_secs()
        )
    })?
    .map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!("Task error: {}", e))??;
```

### Handle Nested Results from Timeouts
```rust
let result = match tokio::time::timeout(timeout::VIDEO_CREATION, video_task).await {
    Ok(Ok(Ok(output_file))) => Ok(output_file),
    Ok(Ok(Err(e))) => Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Failed to create video: {}", e)),
    Ok(Err(e)) => Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Task error: {}", e)),
    Err(_) => Err(anyhow::anyhow!(
        "Video creation timed out after {} minutes",
        timeout::VIDEO_CREATION.as_secs() / 60
    )),
};
```

## 5. Cancellation Error Handling

### Check Cancellation Tokens with Clear Messages
```rust
// Check before starting operation
if let Some(ref token) = cancel_token {
    if is_cancelled(token) {
        anyhow::bail!("Operation cancelled");
    }
}

// Per-item cancellation
if let Some(ref token) = item_cancel_token {
    if token.is_cancelled() {
        return Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Item cancelled"));
    }
}
```

### Cleanup on Cancellation
```rust
if let Some(ref token) = cancel_token {
    if is_cancelled(token) {
        // ALWAYS cleanup temp files on cancellation
        for temp_file in temp_normalized_files {
            let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&temp_file);
        }
        anyhow::bail!("Operation cancelled");
    }
}
```

## 6. Validation Error Patterns

### Use `Result<(), String>` for User-Facing Validation
```rust
pub fn validate_youtube_title(title: &str) -> Result<(), String> {
    let trimmed = title.trim();
    if trimmed.is_empty() {
        return Err("Title cannot be empty".to_string());
    }
    if title.len() > 100 {
        return Err("Title cannot exceed 100 characters".to_string());
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

### Early Return Validation in Commands
```rust
// Validate early in commands with ?
validate_user_path_str(&request.output_path)?;
validate_youtube_title(&request.title)?;
```

## 7. HTTP Error Handling

### Parse HTTP Error Responses Descriptively
```rust
if !status.is_success() {
    let error_text = match response.text().await {
        Ok(text) => text,
        Err(_) => format!("HTTP {} - Could not read error response", status_code)
    };
    
    let error_message = if let Ok(error_json) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(&error_text) {
        let error_code = error_json["error"].as_str().unwrap_or("unknown_error");
        let error_desc = error_json["error_description"]
            .as_str()
            .unwrap_or("No description provided");
        format!("{}: {}", error_code, error_desc)
    } else {
        error_text.clone()
    };
    
    anyhow::bail!("Failed to refresh token (HTTP {}): {}", status_code, error_message);
}
```

## 8. Task/Spawning Error Handling

### Convert Task Join Errors to Descriptive Messages
```rust
let process_result = tokio::time::timeout(timeout::IMAGE_PROCESSING, process_task)
    .await
    .map_err(|_| format!("Image processing timed out after {} seconds", timeout::IMAGE_PROCESSING.as_secs()))
    .and_then(|r| r.map_err(|e| format!("Task error: {}", e)))
    .and_then(|r| r.map_err(|e| format!("Failed to process image: {}", e)));
```

## 9. Error Logging Practices

### Log Errors Before Returning
```rust
match handler.list_folder_contents(&folder_path) {
    Ok(contents) => {
        tracing::debug!("Listed folder contents: {} images, {} audios, {} videos", 
            contents.images.len(), contents.audios.len(), contents.videos.len());
        Ok(contents)
    }
    Err(e) => {
        tracing::error!("Failed to list folder contents for '{}': {}", 
            crate::infrastructure::logging::redact_sensitive(&folder_path), e);
        Err(e.to_string())
    }
}
```

### Log Critical Failures
```rust
if main_path.is_none() && main_url.is_none() {
    tracing::error!("Video creation failed: no image provided");
    anyhow::bail!("No image provided");
}
```

## 10. Bulk Operation Error Handling

### Collect Successes and Failures Separately
```rust
let mut successful = Vec::new();
let mut failed = Vec::new();

for (i, handle) in handles.into_iter().enumerate() {
    match handle.await {
        Ok(Ok(output_file)) => {
            successful.push(output_file);
        }
        Ok(Err(err)) => {
            let audio_path = audio_paths_clone
                .get(i)
                .cloned()
                .unwrap_or_else(|| "unknown".to_string());
            failed.push((audio_path, format!("{}", err)));
        }
        Err(e) => {
            let audio_path = audio_paths_clone
                .get(i)
                .cloned()
                .unwrap_or_else(|| "unknown".to_string());
            failed.push((audio_path, format!("Task error: {}", e)));
        }
    }
}

Ok(BulkVideoResult { successful, failed })
```

## 11. Error Message Quality

### Write Descriptive, User-Friendly Messages
```rust
// ✅ GOOD: Specific and actionable
anyhow::bail!("Not enough disk space. Required: {} MB, Available: {} MB", 
    required_bytes / 1_048_576, available / 1_048_576);

// ✅ GOOD: Includes the failing resource
anyhow::bail!("FFmpeg error: {}", stderr);

// ✅ GOOD: Includes operation context
anyhow::bail!("Failed to create video for {}: {}", audio_path, e);
```

### Avoid Generic Error Messages
```rust
// ❌ BAD: Too generic
anyhow::bail!("Error");

// ❌ BAD: Missing context
anyhow::bail!("Failed");
```

## 12. Error Propagation Rules

### ALWAYS Propagate with Context
```rust
// ✅ GOOD: Propagate with context
let result = some_operation()
    .with_context(|| format!("Failed to process {}", resource))?;
```

### NEVER Ignore or Panic on Errors
```rust
// ❌ BAD: Don't ignore errors
let _ = some_operation();

// ❌ BAD: Don't use unwrap() in production code
let result = some_operation().unwrap();

// ❌ BAD: Don't use expect() unless truly impossible
let result = some_operation().expect("This should never fail");
```

## Summary Checklist

When writing error handling code, ensure:

- [ ] Use `anyhow::Result<T>` in domain/use cases/infrastructure
- [ ] Convert to `Result<T, String>` at command boundaries with `.map_err(|e| e.to_string())`
- [ ] Add meaningful context with `.context()` or `.with_context()`
- [ ] Use `anyhow::bail!()` for early returns and `anyhow::anyhow!()` for error creation
- [ ] Handle timeouts with descriptive timeout duration messages
- [ ] Check cancellation tokens and cleanup resources on cancellation
- [ ] Use `Result<(), String>` for validation functions
- [ ] Parse HTTP errors and provide structured error messages
- [ ] Log errors at appropriate levels before returning
- [ ] Collect successes/failures separately in bulk operations
- [ ] Write specific, actionable error messages with context
- [ ] Never ignore errors or use `unwrap()`/`expect()` in production code

**These patterns ensure consistent, maintainable, and user-friendly error handling across the entire Rust backend.**
